    <h2>What makes Level 33 tricky<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Ten moves, and only two of them are presses: the bag at step one and the window at step seven. Everything else is a drag onto a named person, which makes eight of the ten moves feel like the same gesture. The bag is the first stop and the first trap, because the fan at step two does not exist as a draggable until the bag has been clicked open. A tap on the fan before that produces nothing at all, and a run that starts by hunting the fan sits there tapping at a girl who is only holding a bag.</p>
    <p>The window at step seven is a double-click, and it gates the two moves that follow it. The spray is on the boy's backpack outside the window at step eight, and the flower has to reach the dog outside at step nine. Until that glass has been tapped twice, the two outdoor deliveries are just scenery, so a run that stops around step eight has usually never opened it. Nothing on the frame suggests it opens, which is why the cards put a timestamp on it.</p>
    <p>The pairings do the rest of the damage. Eight drags, eight different recipients, and nothing on screen enforces the match, so the name on each card has to be read before the drag starts. The vacuum cleaner goes to the old lady rather than to the floor it would clean. The lemon leaves the shelf and lands in the girl's bowl on the left at step five, not in her hand. The bill is the one object lifted off a waiter instead of the furniture, and it ends with the child. The plastic bag still sits on the trash can when step ten sends it to the man on the right, which at a glance looks like something to throw away.</p>

    <h2>Ten moves, eight recipients<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The level is a matching exercise with two presses in it, so the mistakes cluster in the same places:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Step 1: click the bag. The fan at step 2 stays untouchable until it is open.</li>
      <li>Step 2: the fan comes out of that bag and goes to the girl on the right.</li>
      <li>Step 3: the vacuum cleaner ends with the old lady, not on the carpet.</li>
      <li>Step 5: the lemon comes off the shelf and into the girl's bowl on the left.</li>
      <li>Step 6: the only object taken from a waiter, delivered to the child.</li>
      <li>Step 7: double-click the window; steps 8 and 9 both reach through it.</li>
      <li>Step 10: the plastic bag leaves the trash can for the man on the right.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Eight drags and two presses, and the ten moves only break when a recipient is guessed instead of read.</p>

    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
   
    <details><summary>What is the answer to Brain Puzzle 3 Level 33?</summary><p>In order: 1) Click the bag of the girl on the left; 2) Drag the fan from the bag to the girl on the right; 3) Drag the vacuum cleaner to the old lady; 4) Drag the umbrella to the boy on the right; 5) Drag the lemon on the shelf to the girl's bowl on the left; 6) Drag the bill from the waiter's hand to the child; 7) Double-click the window; 8) Drag the spray on the boy's backpack outside the window to the creep; 9) Drag the flower on the table to the dog outside the window; 10) Drag the plastic bag on the trash can to the man on the right</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why does nothing happen when I tap in Level 33?</summary><p>Eight of the ten moves are drags onto a named person; only the bag at step one and the window at step seven take a press, and the window needs two of them.</p></details>
